# No in-browser `#agent` feature

The cafe `#agent` LLM / zedcafe-tools product was **removed on purpose**. Do **not** reintroduce it.

## Why it failed

- Large on-device model download and WebGPU inference were slow and unreliable in cafe.
- Main-thread tools plus a separate inference worker added zedcafe write/import sync complexity without a solid product loop.
- Debugging spent more time on model load, tool errors, and zedsync path issues than on useful board edits.
- Opportunity cost: time on `#agent` did not improve the game; rebuilding it repeats that waste.

## Prohibited

- `#agent` CLI / `registeragentcommands` / `zss/firmware/cli/commands/agent.ts`
- `zss/feature/agent/` (or any replacement under another name with the same job)
- `zss/agentspace.ts`, `zss/device/agentworker.ts`, lazy `ensureagentworker`
- Device messages: `register:agentask`, `agent:generate`, `agent:dispose`, `agent:progress`, `agent:error`, `agent:disposed`
- `wanixserver:agentexporttree` / `wanixserver:agentexportwrite` (and matching `wanixclient:*` handlers)

## Allowed (unrelated)

- STT / TTS using `@huggingface/transformers` / ONNX
- Cursor agent-transcripts, IDE agents, FingerprintJS “agent” wording, Wanix submodule “Agent sandboxes”

## Required instead

Edit boards via existing authoring paths (in-sim `#make` / editor, serve-root zedcafe JSON, book templates) — not an in-browser LLM.
